{
  "name": "chameleon",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/chameleon.py): the VEILED CHAMELEON, Chamaeleo calyptratus, a male, 40 cm, the tail half of it. A TALL body FLATTENED FROM SIDE TO SIDE, the back arched, edged with a row of small spines (a serrated `fin`), a pale keel of scales under the throat; a TALL CASQUE (a flat helmet, its rim a ridge) rising from the back of the head; TURRET EYES -- cones of skin on the head's sides, only a small hole at the tip; a short blunt snout and a down-turned mouth; long thin legs held straight DOWN under the body; ZYGODACTYL feet: the toes fused in two opposed bundles splayed apart like tongs (front feet three inward, two outward; hind two inward, three outward), a claw on each; the PREHENSILE TAIL CURLED INTO A SPIRAL (its four bones laid round it, slowly curling). Green, banded on the flanks with yellow and blue-green, a pale stripe low along the side. A slow rocking walk. Coats: veiled, panther chameleon (Furcifer pardalis: turquoise with red bands, .9), common chameleon (olive-brown, .7).",
